What's the implication for the certified order claim? The certified 4-rung order claim is measured from constant-CFL runs (per worker-067/081 F1'). If ladder A is not admissible under symmetric reading, then the certified order claim must come from the fixed-dt ladders B. B ladders at dt=1e-3 and 5e-4 give order 2 within band for all three schemes (from my own verification). But B has 4 rungs (dr 0.2,0.1,0.05,0.025) at each fixed dt — so the ≥4-rung requirement is met.

